explanation: "A £ YES: Some financial monitoring agencies have 500+ staff, and all financial monitoring agencies must submit audits. Thus, those large agencies must submit audits.\nB £ YES: The large financial monitoring agencies are not exempt from transparency mandates and they must submit audits, establishing the overlap.\nC £ NO: We only know transparency status for agencies with 500+ staff. Smaller agencies that submit audits might be exempt from transparency mandates.\nD £ NO: Only 'some' financial monitoring agencies have 500+ staff (making them non-exempt). The remaining ones with fewer staff might be exempt.\nE £ YES: Since no agency with 500+ staff is exempt, it logically follows that any exempt agency must not have 500+ staff."
